// A resource script built for a machine whose loader reads nothing.
//
// The string table travels: it is bytes with a number on it, and
// `Standard.Resources` reads it identically on every target. The manifest does
// not, in the sense that matters -- it is carried and readable, and nothing
// outside Windows turns one into a side-by-side assembly binding. SL0700 names
// the second and says nothing about the first.
STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    1 "this reaches an ELF binary and can be read there"
END

1 24 "skipped.manifest"
